{"name": "snRNAseq on trained and untrained human skeletal muscle from healthy donors", "description": "Single-nuclei RNA sequencing (snRNA-seq) data of human muscle cells. The samples are a part of a study investigating the effect of one-legged high-intensity interval training (HIIT) on the nuclear transcriptional response in skeletal muscle. The HIIT was done on one leg on a cycle ergometer, and vastus lateralis muscle biopsies were obtained from both the untrained and trained leg following the two weeks training protocol. This subset of data from 10 samples of healthy individuals. These healthy donors were from a Body Mass Index (BMI) and age matched control group without diabetes. The healthy donors were matched to 9 people with Type 2 Diabetes (T2D). The T2D samples are not included in this data subset). The experimental study is described in: Dela et al., Acta Physiol, 2019. The snRNA-seq data contains nuclei isolated from 20 available biopsies of a trained and untrained leg.", "cellCount": 52597, "geneCount": 31087, "labelsets": [{"name": "organism", "description": null, "annotationMethod": null, "algorithmName": null, "algorithmVersion": null, "algorithmRepoUrl": null, "referenceLocation": null, "referenceDescription": null, "mode": "metadata", "status": "parsed", "labelCount": null, "order": null, "labels": [{"name": "Homo sapiens", "count": 52597, "color": "#db5f57", "fullName": null, "ontologyTermExists": null, "ontologyTermId": "NCBITaxon:9606", "ontologyTerm": null, "rationale": null, "rationaleDois": null, "markerGenes": null, "canonicalMarkerGenes": null, "synonyms": null, "categoryFullName": null, "categoryOntologyTermExists": null, "categoryOntologyTermId": null, "categoryOntologyTerm": null, "ontologyAssessment": null, "averageConfScore": null}]}, {"name": "tissue", "description": null, "annotationMethod": null, "algorithmName": null, "algorithmVersion": null, "algorithmRepoUrl": null, "referenceLocation": null, "referenceDescription": null, "mode"